timestamp=2026-11-04T15:43:38.950Z level=INFO run=258c00cc message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# Look at who claims for whom based on patterns\n# \"family support adjustment\" and \"bereavement compensation\" often follow death\n# Also look at patients who have no claims themselves, but someone they are EC for also has no claims? Or weird chains\n\n# build full network\npatient_has_claim = {}\nfor r in rows:\n    pid = r['patient_id']\n    if r['record_date'].strip():\n        patient_has_claim[pid] = True\nfor r in rows:\n    pid = r['patient_id']\n    if pid not in patient_has_claim:\n        patient_has_claim[pid] = False\n\n# for claims by \"family support adjustment\" or \"bereavement\", who is the subject?\n# maybe the EC is the claimant filing for the patient? Or the patient in the row is the claimant?\n# look at amounts and context\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['compensation_reason'] in ('family support adjustment', 'bereavement compensation'):\n        print(r)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
