timestamp=2026-11-04T15:44:52.488Z level=INFO run=258c00cc message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\npatient_has_claim = {}\nfor r in rows:\n    pid = r['patient_id']\n    if r['record_date'].strip():\n        patient_has_claim[pid] = True\nfor r in rows:\n    pid = r['patient_id']\n    if pid not in patient_has_claim:\n        patient_has_claim[pid] = False\n\n# look at patients with serious claims: who might be deceased?\n# if someone files bereavement/family support, maybe the person being supported is deceased?\n# also look at who lists who as EC and the direction\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['compensation_reason'] == 'bereavement compensation':\n        # PAT_033 (Reese Rivera) has this claim. They are alive? They have a claim themselves. Also their EC is PAT_011.\n        # Or maybe the subject is someone else? \"bereavement compensation\" could mean for the death of someone\n        pass\n\n# look up more context\n# PAT_033's EC is PAT_011. Who is PAT_011?\nfor pid in ['PAT_011', 'PAT_065', 'PAT_078']:\n    print(f'\\n=== {pid} ===')\n    for r in rows:\n        if r['patient_id'] == pid:\n            print(r)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
