timestamp=2026-11-04T15:46:15.719Z level=INFO run=258c00cc message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# look for other signals: coverage_status inactive for EC filing serious claims? or policy tier\n# also look at patients with no claims who are EC for someone else, and maybe the someone else is also in a bad state? Or look for \"life event claim\" again carefully\n# or look for chains where the no-claim patient's EC has trauma and also the no-claim patient is referenced in other ways\n\n# Also consider: sometimes the deceased person might have their own record but no claims? Or they just don't exist as claimant\n# Another angle: look at all patients with no claims. Also look at who they list as EC. If their EC files a claim with large direct_payment_usd for serious reasons, and the patient has no claims themselves, likely deceased\npatient_has_claim = {}\nfor r in rows:\n    pid = r['patient_id']\n    if r['record_date'].strip():\n        patient_has_claim[pid] = True\nfor r in rows:\n    pid = r['patient_id']\n    if pid not in patient_has_claim:\n        patient_has_claim[pid] = False\n\nno_claim = set(k for k,v in patient_has_claim.items() if not v)\nresults = []\nfor pid in no_claim:\n    rlist = [x for x in rows if x['patient_id'] == pid]\n    if not rlist: continue\n    r = rlist[0]\n    ec = r['emergency_contact_patient_id']\n    score = 0\n    ec_claim_reasons = []\n    for rr in rows:\n        if rr['patient_id'] == ec and rr['record_date'].strip():\n            ec_claim_reasons.append(rr['compensation_reason'])\n            if rr['compensation_reason'] in ('bereavement compensation', 'family support adjustment', 'life event claim'):\n                score += 100\n            elif rr['compensation_reason'] in ('vehicle crash injury', 'workplace fall injury', 'burn injury'):\n                score += 5\n    results.append((pid, score, ec, ec_claim_reasons))\n\nresults.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)\nfor x in results[:5]:\n    print(x)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
