timestamp=2026-11-04T15:46:23.671Z level=INFO run=258c00cc message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\n# look more at others with trauma - are there any with serious claims?\n# also check if the \"no claims yet\" patients - could be they are minors or just haven't filed? \n# but combined with EC filing bereavement/family support is a strong indicator of death\n\n# also look at PAT_040 (who lists PAT_023 as EC) and PAT_032 (who lists PAT_174 as EC) - they themselves have no claims. \n# That suggests the structure: the person who might normally be contact is gone?\n# Also look at direct payments - bereavement/family support have large amounts\n\n# only 2 clear cases from serious claims. Are there exactly 3 patients total expected?\n# the task says \"Return a set of three patient IDs that are most likely to be deceased.\"\n# so we need exactly 3. Maybe look for the next best signals?\n\n# another pattern: patient has no claims, and their EC has trauma claims. Also the patient might be listed as EC for someone who also has no claims? Or other dependents have no claims\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
